A peak load plant must start in minutes and have a low capital cost; a high fuel cost does not matter because it runs only a few hours.

- Nuclear and steam: slow to start, high capital cost → base load.
- Hydro: depends on the type (run-of-river is base load; only storage hydro suits peaks).
- **Gas turbine:** starts in minutes, cheapest to build, costly fuel: the textbook peak load plant.

**Answer: (D) Gas turbine power plant.**
