', '**Idea used:** reaction turbines — see *Hydroelectric power plants → Impulse and reaction turbines*.

A reaction turbine''s runner is completely filled with water in a closed casing and is driven by the drop of pressure across it. An impulse turbine (Pelton) is driven by a free jet in open air at atmospheric pressure, so its runner is not embedded in the water and there is no pressure drop across it. "Squirrel cage" is an induction-motor rotor, not a turbine.

**Answer: (B) Reaction turbine only.**
