    VALUES (subj, tid, 'NUMERICAL', 'A station''s fixed charges are ₹43.8 crore per year. Its maximum demand is 50 MW and its annual load factor is 0.5. The fixed cost per kWh generated is', 'A station''s fixed charges are ₹43.8 crore per year. Its maximum demand is 50 MW and its annual load factor is 0.5. The fixed cost per kWh generated is
', '**Idea used:** fixed cost per unit = fixed charges ÷ ($P_m\times LF\times8760$) — see *Cost of generation and tariffs → Cost per unit and the load factor*.

Energy $= 50\,000\times0.5\times8760 = 25\,000\times8760 = 21.9\times10^7$ kWh. Cost per unit $= 43.8\times10^7/21.9\times10^7 = ₹2$.

**Answer: (C) ₹2.00.**
', 'READY', 'MCQ', NULL, NULL, 2, 'REVIEWED', 'ps1-q-024', 'PRACTICE') RETURNING id INTO qid;
